    "blurb": "Calculate SLA deadlines across business calendars",
    "overview": "The Advance Calendar Connector calculates a target date by advancing or moving backward from a starting date by a specified duration in hours or days, taking into account business hours, public holidays by country, and time zone differences. Use it to calculate SLA deadlines that respect the actual working hours of your team rather than raw calendar time.",
    "rating": null,
    "reviewCount": 0,
    "mobileBundleId": null,
    "mobileAppStoreId": null
  },
  "overview": {
    "splashTitle": "Calculate calendar date for SLA, taking into account custom calendar and holidays",
    "splashDescription": "SLA deadlines like \"resolve within 40 business hours\" are only meaningful if the calculation reflects when your team is actually working — not raw elapsed time. The Advance Calendar Connector calculates a target date by advancing or moving backward from a starting date by a given duration, skipping non-business hours and public holidays by country. It supports two modes: hours mode advances time within your configured open hours (for example, 09:00–18:00), and days mode counts only business days. Time zone differences between the requester and the handling office are handled automatically, so the deadline is always expressed correctly for both sides. Configure your business calendar and holiday region through process variables, and the connector returns the adjusted date ready for use in any downstream step.",
    "imageUrl": "https://d3bql97l1ytoxn.cloudfront.net/app_resources/808470/overview/img8532833209650465250.png?f2a59b445cca0e2cd69b70c8a125e1a2",
